ke screen time on my phone  it set my screen time that week compared  to the week before I did the experiment  was down by 75% that's insane  that is hours of one's life that you  could be investing in work and when you  know ultimately time is money when  you're an entrepreneur  that is really valuable stuff I mean I  would way rather spend all that extra  time with my family of course but just  to think about it that way kind of like  as a transaction was really eye-opening  to me now this is the miraculous thing I  don't know why and I don't know how but  just not feeling so plugged in really  did help me get a better sleep  I went from maybe getting like two good  nights of sleep a week to going to like  five and from just that that one change  alone it was that powerful honestly I  would never have let myself you know  look at my phone past 7:00 p.m. because  of the screen time rules and all that  stuff but just not having those social  media apps operating in the background  it just didn't leave me so hyper  stimulated by the time I was trying to  wind down and go to sleep and I wasn't  constantly worrying about what was going  on or what I was missing out on it was  life changing okay so how am i balancing  social media in my own life right now  well like I said this was ultimately an  experiment and while I totally  appreciate that a lot of people go and  have these social media Detox's and they  realize like how much they hate social  media I actually realized that  ultimately I still really like it I love  the like storytelling aspect of it and I  also really love the genuine  interactions with all of you but I also  knew that I really did need to set some  boundaries so after two weeks without  any social media on my phone I decided I  need to set some you know a little bit  of a curfew with my social media usage I  ended up downloading like a dozen  different apps all promising to kind of  help one control their social media  addiction but unfortunately 